The method `StDistance.processGeoSourceAndSource` now takes a `DoubleBlock.Builder` and directly appends the result. Ensure that this change does not introduce any issues with how results are being appended to the block.
```java
try {
    StDistance.processGeoSourceAndSource(result, p, leftBlock, rightBlock);
} catch (IllegalArgumentException e) {
    warnings().registerException(e);
    result.appendNull();
}
```

The addition of `SPATIAL_DISTANCE_SUPPORTS_MULTIVALUES` and the modification in `EnableSpatialDistancePushdown#rewrite` suggest that multi-value support has been added. Ensure that this change is thoroughly tested to cover all scenarios involving multi-values.
```java
if (rewritten.equals(filterExec.condition()) == false && canPushToSource(rewritten, x -> false)) {
    return new FilterExec(filterExec.source(), esQueryExec, rewritten);
}
```

The multi-value checks for `leftBlock` and `rightBlock` have been removed. Ensure that this change is intentional, as it might lead to incorrect results if the blocks contain multiple values.
```java
if (leftBlock.getValueCount(p) != 1 || rightBlock.getValueCount(p) != 1) {
    warnings().registerException(new IllegalArgumentException("single-value function encountered multi-value"));
    result.appendNull();
    continue position;
}
```

The logic for handling null values has been simplified but introduces a new variable `allBlocksAreNulls`. This could be made more concise by directly checking if both blocks are null within the same condition.
```java
if (leftBlock.isNull(p) && rightBlock.isNull(p)) {
    result.appendNull();
    continue position;
}
```

The cast of coordinates to `float` is done to mimic Lucene's behavior. Ensure that this change does not introduce precision issues or unexpected results.
```java
final double diffX = (float) left.getX() - (float) right.getX();
final double diffY = (float) left.getY() - (float) right.getY();
```

